{"obsah":"<p>Our farewell to the Tehov park before winter – and hopefully its spring rebuild – in the form of small races and training was moved a bit. There was a risk that few riders would come because of the long weekend, but in the end the turnout was a surprise. About 20 riders started in Trial and a similar number on the pump track, which is about half of the club's members. The weather was for tougher characters – alternately muddy, but without rain – but the kids didn't mind and the adult riders survived too 🙂</p>\n\n<p>As every year, the rules were based on OPEN FREE, with riders choosing the arrows they want to ride and the difficulty. Categories were divided by age and, for older riders, by riders. Each rider had to adapt the course to themselves with a limit of 5–6 arrows per section. Riding was in groups, each with its own judge, who could also adjust the rules to suit the riders.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>It was great that a few club legends who don't normally come to training showed up too. Michal Havránek got up from his director's chair, saddled his blue Ozonys and battled more with his physical fitness – which, as he said, he needs to catch up on – than with the bike. Martin Šimůnek rode his last big event on a 24” before switching to 26”, on which he won a number of world titles, and he really surprised in his duel with Míra Brunclík. Honestly, doing gaps onto around 10–11 pallets in the mud after turning 50 is insane, and on one of the sections in the first round Míra and Martin even managed to beat Mára and Vlasta. At the other end of the age spectrum, a Martin also cleverly took 3rd place – but this one from the Gomboš family.</p>\n\n<p>The rules were very much about using your head and thinking, so even a rider weaker in jumping or performance could beat a more experienced one if they attempted harder arrows – and the results showed it. 5 riders entered on 20” bikes and the same number on 26”. Tobík Dolák won Elite 20” just ahead of his 20-inch guru Valňák, and Vlasta battled Mára Tryner for first place on the 26-inch bikes.</p>\n\n<p>The pump track followed straight after, so the Trial riders had time to change clothes and bikes. After a few practice runs, the youngest riders on balance bikes started, and then it went all the way up to the fastest adults.</p>\n\n<p>The finale was all about tidying up and sausages.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F11%2FDSC_9743-scaled.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F11%2FDSC_9743.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-249940\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F11%2FDSC_9746-scaled.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F11%2FDSC_9746.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-249939\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F11%2FDSC_9759-scaled.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F11%2FDSC_9759.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-249938\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F11%2FDSC_9768-scaled.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fupload